  "title": "A subset of large-scale EEG dataset (India + Tanzania)",
  "description": "A subset of a large-scale field EEG collection from India and Tanzania, including participants ranging from Hadzabe hunter-gatherers to office workers. Recordings are accompanied by metadata such as age, Mental Health Quotient (MHQ) score, income and sex. The parent program used trained nonspecialist teams and daily automated data-quality feedback to collect EEG at high throughput and low cost, with quality comparable to lab benchmark datasets.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was collected in the field by trained nonspecialist research teams alongside surveys and assessments. Data quality was evaluated with the PREP and FASTER pipelines. The BIDS dataset was generated from EDF source files using MNE-BIDS.",
